PHP 7.4 ext/intl: ask ICU for C++17 when ICU needs it (upstream's own probe)

Taken from php-src PHP-8.3's ext/intl/config.m4, applied to 7.4 because 7.4 is
end-of-life and never received it.

7.4 hardcodes `PHP_CXX_COMPILE_STDCXX(11, mandatory, PHP_INTL_STDCXX)`. ICU 74+
headers use C++14/17 in their public API, so compiling intl against a modern ICU
under C++11 fails in ICU's own headers:

    buildroot/include/unicode/char16ptr.h:271:38:
      error: no template named 'enable_if_t' in namespace 'std'
    buildroot/include/unicode/char16ptr.h:271:55:
      error: no template named 'is_same_v' in namespace 'std'
    make: *** [ext/intl/intl_convertcpp.lo] Error 1

Setting CXXFLAGS from outside does NOT fix it, which is the part worth knowing:
PHP_CXX_COMPILE_STDCXX appends its own `-std=` to the intl-specific flag set
after ours, so `-std=c++11` wins no matter what the environment says. The
standard has to change where intl chooses it.

Upstream's fix probes ICU rather than hardcoding the newer standard, and the
probe is kept verbatim: with an older ICU this stays on C++11 exactly as before,
so the patch cannot break a build that was working.

Verified against php-src PHP-8.3.31 ext/intl/config.m4 (lines 84-91).

--- a/ext/intl/config.m4	2026-08-14 23:07:42
+++ b/ext/intl/config.m4	2026-08-14 23:07:42
@@ -83,7 +83,14 @@
     breakiterator/codepointiterator_methods.cpp"
 
   PHP_REQUIRE_CXX()
-  PHP_CXX_COMPILE_STDCXX(11, mandatory, PHP_INTL_STDCXX)
+  AC_MSG_CHECKING([if intl requires -std=gnu++17])
+  AS_IF([$PKG_CONFIG icu-uc --atleast-version=74],[
+    AC_MSG_RESULT([yes])
+    PHP_CXX_COMPILE_STDCXX(17, mandatory, PHP_INTL_STDCXX)
+  ],[
+    AC_MSG_RESULT([no])
+    PHP_CXX_COMPILE_STDCXX(11, mandatory, PHP_INTL_STDCXX)
+  ])
   PHP_INTL_CXX_FLAGS="$INTL_COMMON_FLAGS $PHP_INTL_STDCXX $ICU_CXXFLAGS"
   if test "$ext_shared" = "no"; then
     PHP_ADD_SOURCES(PHP_EXT_DIR(intl), $PHP_INTL_CXX_SOURCES, $PHP_INTL_CXX_FLAGS)
